From: FiyeroT <me@fiyero.xyz>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 21:41:21 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 55/60] box: StartWithoutClose leaves a box whose start failed
 to its caller

StartWithoutClose leaves a box whose start failed to its caller.

Made of these commits of the earlier series (branch archive/r25-1.14-commits):
  6d546710b box: StartWithoutClose leaves a box whose start failed to its caller

Pdk-Feature: box-start
Pdk-Zone: other
Pdk-Layer: 04
---
 box.go | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/box.go b/box.go
index d9d90b90f..60e450dbd 100644
--- a/box.go
+++ b/box.go
@@ -504,6 +504,17 @@ func (s *Box) PreStart() error {
 }
 
 func (s *Box) Start() error {
+	err := s.StartWithoutClose()
+	if err != nil {
+		s.Close()
+	}
+	return err
+}
+
+// StartWithoutClose is Start that leaves a box whose start failed as it is: the caller
+// closes it, and may bound how long that takes (podkop-engine). Start closes it at once,
+// and a component whose Close does not return holds Start with it.
+func (s *Box) StartWithoutClose() error {
 	err := s.start()
 	if err != nil {
 		return err
-- 
